  displayName: Mackerel
  scientificName: Scomber scombrus
  description: A fast-swimming pelagic fish with iridescent blue-green stripes and
    a streamlined body built for speed. Mackerel often travel in large schools that
    shimmer as they change direction.
  depthLayer: 
  behavior: Forms tightly packed schools in open water above the kelp canopy. The
    school moves as a coordinated group, rapidly turning and changing shape in response
    to threats.
